# Derived by hand under ruling PL (the `for` is the page's 0, each name's row holds the `rebuild` at its 0, generation #0, the teller applied there with a list of its own, its button 0 and label 1) from Type System ch. 3 (a widget read at a type is the widget at that type) and Semantics ch. 4 (a hold's next value is read in its event's tick): each teller's click says the quiet order's words for its first click; the loud order, called at its own type, says its own.
test each_says_by_its_type

tick 0
  added:
    0.["ada"].0.#0.0/0: Ui.Button(label="ada")
    0.["ada"].0.#0.0/1: Ui.Label(text="ada: nothing yet")
    0.["bob"].0.#0.0/0: Ui.Button(label="bob")
    0.["bob"].0.#0.0/1: Ui.Label(text="bob: nothing yet")
    1: Ui.Label(text="loud says CLICKED 1")

tick 1
  in:
    0.["ada"].0.#0.0/0: click
  changed:
    0.["ada"].0.#0.0/1: Ui.Label(text="ada: clicked 1")

tick 2
  in:
    0.["bob"].0.#0.0/0: click
  changed:
    0.["bob"].0.#0.0/1: Ui.Label(text="bob: clicked 1")
